From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: poll FN_READY after enabling a function

sdio_enable_func() set the CCCR IOEx bit and returned immediately.  The
SDIO specification (5.1) has the card report readiness back through IORx
(SD_IO_CCCR_FN_READY), which can lag the enable by a noticeable time;
Linux's sdio_enable_func() polls it for up to a second before returning.

Without the poll a caller can start driving a function that has been told
to come up but has not yet, and sees bare CMD52 response timeouts with
nothing to explain them.  On a BCM43430 the readiness bit was observed to
take 7-21ms for function 2, so this is not a theoretical window.

Poll IORx with a 1ms granularity and a 1s timeout.

Signed-off-by: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sys/dev/sdio/sdio_subr.c b/sys/dev/sdio/sdio_subr.c
index f234eb8bd..25504ad9d 100644
--- a/sys/dev/sdio/sdio_subr.c
+++ b/sys/dev/sdio/sdio_subr.c
@@ -97,9 +97,38 @@ sdio_set_bool_for_func(device_t dev, uint32_t addr, uint8_t fn, bool enable)
 int
 sdio_enable_func(struct sdio_func *f)
 {
+	device_t pdev;
+	int error;
+	uint8_t val;
+	int timeout_ms = 1000;
 
-	return (sdio_set_bool_for_func(f->dev, SD_IO_CCCR_FN_ENABLE,
-	    f->fn, true));
+	error = sdio_set_bool_for_func(f->dev, SD_IO_CCCR_FN_ENABLE,
+	    f->fn, true);
+	if (error != 0)
+		return (error);
+
+	/*
+	 * Setting IOEx only asks the card to bring the function up; the SDIO
+	 * spec (5.1) has the card signal readiness back via IORx (CCCR
+	 * SD_IO_CCCR_FN_READY), which can take a while after enable. Linux's
+	 * sdio_enable_func() polls this bit before returning; this one
+	 * didn't, so callers (e.g. brcmfmac's F1 backplane-window writes
+	 * right after enabling F1) could run against a function that had
+	 * been told to come up but hadn't yet, and see plain CMD52 response
+	 * timeouts with no indication why. Poll here instead.
+	 */
+	pdev = device_get_parent(f->dev);
+	for (;;) {
+		error = SDIO_READ_DIRECT(pdev, 0, SD_IO_CCCR_FN_READY, &val);
+		if (error != 0)
+			return (error);
+		if (val & (1 << f->fn))
+			return (0);
+		if (timeout_ms <= 0)
+			return (ETIMEDOUT);
+		DELAY(1000);
+		timeout_ms--;
+	}
 }
 
 int
